<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<addon
  id="inputstream.airplay"
  version="0.1.6"
  name="AirPlay Receiver"
  provider-name="popcornmix">
  <requires>@ADDON_DEPENDS@
    <import addon="xbmc.python" version="3.0.1"/>
  </requires>
  <extension
    point="kodi.inputstream"
    name="airplay"
    protocols="airplay"
    extension=""
    tags="true"
    library_@PLATFORM@="@LIBRARY_FILENAME@"/>
  <extension
    point="xbmc.service"
    library="default.py"/>
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <platform>@PLATFORM@</platform>
    <license>GPL-3.0-or-later</license>
    <source>https://github.com/popcornmix/inputstream.airplay</source>
    <assets>
      <icon>icon.png</icon>
    </assets>
    <news>Accepts H.265 mirroring, which is what a phone sends to a 4K display -- without it mirroring failed outright on those. The receiver writes to the add-on from a thread of its own, so a slow consumer no longer stalls the protocol. Video handed over from a browser starts where the phone was and plays rather than sitting paused, and stopping playback locally is noticed by the phone.</news>
    <summary lang="en_GB">Mirror an iPhone or iPad screen to Kodi</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">Receives AirPlay screen mirroring, video streamed from apps, and audio, and plays them through Kodi's own pipeline, so hardware decoding and the normal renderer are used.

Video protected by DRM cannot be received: the sender blanks it before it leaves the phone.</description>
  </extension>
</addon>
